From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build: add a docs option

docs/meson.build starts with find_program('itstool'), and subdir('docs') is
not conditional, so a build with no itstool on the machine stops at configure:

  docs/meson.build:1:6: ERROR: Program 'itstool' not found or not executable

Every other optional part of the tree can be switched off - xdmcp, plymouth,
selinux, libaudit, x11-support, wayland-support - but the manual cannot, so a
build that wants only libgdm has to bring in a documentation toolchain to get
it.

Add a docs option, defaulting true so nothing changes for anyone building the
whole thing.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gdm/-/issues
Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 option('defaults-conf', type: 'string', value: '', description: 'Filename to give to defaults file.')
 option('distro', type: 'string', value: 'none', description: 'Distribution name, used to detect PAM files and hook scripts.')
 option('dmconfdir', type: 'string', value: '', description: 'Directory where sessions are stored.')
+option('docs', type: 'boolean', value: true, description: 'Build the documentation, which needs itstool.')
 option('gdm-xsession', type: 'boolean', value: false, description: 'Enable installing the gdm Xsession file.')
 option('gnome-settings-daemon-dir', type: 'string', value: '', description: 'Specify the directory of gnome-settings-daemon used by the chooser.')
 option('group', type: 'string', value: 'gdm', description: 'GDM\'s group.')
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -323,7 +323,9 @@
 if have_xdmcp
   subdir('chooser')
 endif
-subdir('docs')
+if get_option('docs')
+  subdir('docs')
+endif
 
 gnome.post_install(
   glib_compile_schemas: true,
